    "certitude": "hypothetique",
    "mode": "terre",
    "description": "On the orders of Intendant Talon, Jolliet sets out with Jean Péré to explore the copper mines of Lake Superior, of which the missionaries have brought back samples. He takes the trade canoe route: the Ottawa, the Mattawa, Lake Nipissing and the French River, then Georgian Bay and Sault Ste. Marie.",
    "sources": "Gagnon, Louis Jolliet (2e éd., 1913), p. 43-47.",
    "note": "Route reconstructed along the usual canoe route; the end point on Lake Superior is symbolic.",
    "type": "trajet"
