    "certitude": "certaine",
    "mode": "fleuve",
    "description": "For a month the canoes descend the Mississippi, from 42 and a half degrees to about 33 degrees. They pass the painted rocks of the Piasa, the turbulent mouth of the Pekitanouï (Missouri), Tower Rock and the Ouabouskigou (Ohio). Farther south come the canebrakes and the mosquitoes, then the villages of Mitchigamea and Akansea, armed with muskets.",
